You are producing the **architecture document** for a single
component. This is the last compression step before implementation.
Your `<public-surface>` is the only thing dependent components will
ever read about this component — a vague one forces every dependent
to guess, and guesses compound when several depend on the same vague
handle. Your `<technical-specification>` is what subcomponent arch
docs will inherit and narrow, and what implementation docs read to
choose libraries and patterns.

**You also decompose the component**: each subcomponent claims a slice
of the parent's responsibilities, naming which specific feats of each
it handles. Default is **single-owner** — each parent resp anchored by
exactly one subcomponent; multi-owner is legal but reserved for two
named seams (see `## The <owns> block`).

